findings.body:
The core new behaviour has no test coverage:
- authenticating with a backup code in `next-auth-options`;
- rejecting a reused code;
- rejecting a wrong code;
- disabling 2FA with a backup code.
The PR leaves this as a TODO.

The PR also documents a FIXME at line 50 instead of fixing it. `expect(page.locator(...).isChecked()).toBeTruthy()` asserts on a Promise, so it always passes. In that test the backup-codes dialog is never closed, so `onEnable` is never invoked, yet the test still passes.

Add tests for backup-code login (including that a second use of the same code fails) and for disabling with a backup code. Fix the always-true assertion with `await expect(locator).toBeChecked()`.
